# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Model providers for the agent layer.
#
# At least ONE key is required for agents 1-3, 5 and 6. Agent 4 (Narrative)
# degrades to the deterministic rules-engine explanation without any key, and
# every non-agent feature works regardless.
#
# Runs walk the chain in order, so a free-tier rate limit falls through to the
# next provider instead of ending the session.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# RECOMMENDED PRIMARY — free, no card, 1M-token context, native structured
# output. Best free-tier tool calling, which is what agents 1, 2, 5 and 6 need.
# Get one at https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=

# FAST LANE — ~1M tokens/day free, no card. Primary for the Narrative agent
# because it has no tools and a closed prompt, so speed matters more than depth.
# https://cloud.cerebras.ai
CEREBRAS_API_KEY=

# RATE-LIMIT INSURANCE — free tier with tight per-minute limits, so it sits
# second rather than first. https://console.groq.com
GROQ_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL, OFFLINE — runs on your own machine, free forever.
# Deliberately last in the chain: a laptop-sized model is not reliable for
# multi-step tool chains or strict JSON schemas. Fine for narrative work.
#   brew install ollama && ollama pull llama3.1:8b
# OLLAMA_MODEL=llama3.1:8b
# OLLAMA_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:11434/api

# OPTIONAL, PAID — routes to frontier models through one key.
# Takes priority when present. https://vercel.com/docs/ai-gateway
# AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY=
